\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The problem. Two locations have been evaluated and returned equal values (dots); the shaded region is the posterior band, the dashed curve the posterior median $e^{\mu }$ and the solid curve the posterior mean $e^{\mu +\nu /2}$. The final evaluation is the consequential one: settle between the anchors, step out past an end, or stay at an observed point. The paper computes which, exactly, as a function of the anchor value and the bracket correlation.}}{6}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:problem}{{1}{6}{The problem. Two locations have been evaluated and returned equal values (dots); the shaded region is the posterior band, the dashed curve the posterior median $e^{\mu }$ and the solid curve the posterior mean $e^{\mu +\nu /2}$. The final evaluation is the consequential one: settle between the anchors, step out past an end, or stay at an observed point. The paper computes which, exactly, as a function of the anchor value and the bracket correlation}{figure.1}{}}
